    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222-a1">

                <pb facs="1095" n="1068" xml:id="pg1068"/>


                <head>Paper Prepared in the Soviet Ministry of Foreign Affairs<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d222-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Moscow</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian">undated</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Pursuant to the agreement reached in Geneva we are making vigorous efforts on our
                    part to intensify the process of completing the START Treaty. President Bush’s
                    message has been reported to President Gorbachev, and intensive work is now
                    under way to prepare our response. We expect that President Gorbachev’s message
                    shall be ready by the end of the week. With this in mind, we shall be promptly
                    notifying the Secretary of State as to when Mr. Obukhov shall be ready, on the
                    basis of US and our own ideas, to have a discussion with R. Bartholomew and let
                    me note that the Minister strongly supports the idea of Mr. Bartholomew’s coming
                    to Geneva on an urgent basis.</p>
                <p>As early as tomorrow we shall be sending a group of our experts to Geneva to
                    discuss telemetry issues. In this connection, we expect to receive shortly
                    relevant detailed US proposals.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d222-f1" n="4" type="source" xml:id="d222-f1-content">
                <p>Secret. An unknown hand wrote at the top of the paper: “Oral message from A.
                    Bessmertnykh to Secretary J. Baker.” A stamped notation indicates Scowcroft saw
                    the paper. The Russian text of the paper is ibid.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
